Fixes review reminder emails sent with a raw ":deferred:<hash>:" token and without inlined CSS
after the Magento 2026-10-001 security patch (APSB26-153).

Root cause: the magento/framework 248p5-2026-10-001 / 249-2026-10-001 patch makes child templates
(e.g. {{template config_path="design/email/header_template"}}) defer their {{inlinecss}} directive
to the root template through the shared DeferredDirectiveRegistry and leave a ":deferred:<hash>:"
placeholder in their output. Core Template::filter() resolves those placeholders when the shared
FilteringDepthMeter is at depth 1. Aheadworks\ReviewReminder\Model\Template\Filter overrides
filter() without calling the parent, so it never moves the depth meter and never resolves the
registry: the header child template runs at depth 1, defers the directive to itself and the
placeholder ends up in the sent email.
Fix: filter() descends and ascends the shared FilteringDepthMeter and, at depth 1, resolves the
deferred directives before running the after filter callbacks, mirroring core Template::filter().
The meter is ascended in "finally", because filter() swallows exceptions and a meter left raised
would stop every following email of the same cron run from resolving its placeholders.

Gotcha: forDirective() filters each loop body through process(). Resolving the deferred directives
inside process() (as the build-artifacts hotfix af2e5c44 did) clears the registry while the
{{for item in order.getAllVisibleItems()}} body is processed - after the header was deferred but
before the root resolves it - so the placeholder still leaks. Every review reminder template has
such a loop. process() is therefore split into processDirectives() and the after filter step, and
deferred directives are resolved only once, in filter(), for the whole document. Loop bodies keep
their original behaviour.

Requires the magento/framework 248p5-2026-10-001 or 249-2026-10-001 patch: without it
\Magento\Framework\Filter\Template\DeferredDirectiveRegistry does not exist.

